      "id": "survey-akari-acua",
      "subject": "AKARI thermal diameter as an alternative scale",
      "status": "excluded",
      "finding": "[AKARI AcuA](https://data.darts.isas.jaxa.jp/pub/akari/AKARI-IRC_Catalogue_AllSky_AcuA_1.0/) — retained for comparison; the documented physical calibration supplies the selected scale. Its fitted nonrotating-sphere diameter is 82.97 ± 0.81 km. Formal catalog error omits additional shape, spin and thermal-model effects; no total confidence interval is invented. The original catalogue row for asteroid 110 was retrieved again and matched field-for-field with the retained row, including diameter, reported error and detection count.",
